# Vectorize Semantic Search Architecture

## Overview

Six Cloudflare Vectorize indexes provide semantic (conceptual) search across all user content. Embeddings are generated via Workers AI (`@cf/baai/bge-small-en-v1.5`, 384-dim, free with Workers Paid $5/mo). Write-path embedding happens fire-and-forget on every content insertion. Read-path queries support both backend-side (Python → REST API) and edge-side (Worker → Vectorize binding).

## Recall Optimizations

### BGE Query Instruction Prefix (Free +1-2% nDCG)

All query-time embedding calls prepend `"Represent this sentence for searching relevant passages: "` to the search query. This is the BGE model's designed asymmetric behavior — documents are embedded without prefix, queries WITH prefix. Applied in `semantic_search()`, `semantic_search_family()`, `semantic_search_group()`, and the edge Worker's `handleSemanticSearch()`.

### Structured Clinical Photo Annotations

Photo analysis uses `CLINICAL_PHOTO_PROMPT` in `vectorize_service.py` with structured headers (PEOPLE, EMOTIONS, SETTING, OBJECTS, DYNAMICS, THERAPEUTIC THEMES, COLORS & ATMOSPHERE). Each section is independently searchable via its embedding. Used by both unified search auto-analysis and vault photo analysis.

### Image-to-Image Search via Vision LLM

`image_to_image_search()` uses Workers AI `llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct` to describe a query image, then embeds that description for semantic search against `nate-annotations`. No CLIP or new infrastructure needed.

### Granular Metadata Filtering

All write paths inject `family_id`, `group_id`, `company_id`, `tier` from the user's profile. Queries use these for scoped searches (family, group, company). At 1M users, this reduces index scan from billions to thousands of vectors per query.

